'various' and Chinese variety expressions are strongest; 'any', 'some',
'each', etc. are weaker. Local rules distinguish collective noun + 'of',
'the following', 'a few', and 'each other'. Completed byte-split Chinese
characters are recognized from the causal decoded prefix. The previous word
and its strength reset at document changes. Elsewhere the prediction is zero;
many small vocabulary-specific responses are deliberately omitted.
